{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cice_thermodynamics",
  "description": "CICE column thermodynamics (stage 2 of the EqESM project): the per-category vertical heat conduction, surface energy balance, and growth/melt closures of the D-class run configuration of cesm3_cice6_6_3_22 (ktherm = 2 mushy, shortwave = 'dEdd', frzpnd = 'hlid' sea-level ponds, nilyr = 8, nslyr = 3, phi_i_mushy = 0.45, hs0 = 0.0, snwredist = 'none', use_smliq_pnd = .false., congel_freeze = 'one-step', saltflux_option = 'constant', tfrz_option = 'mushy', conduct = 'MU71', dpscale = 1e-3, vapor_flux_correction = .false.), written over the ncat thickness categories and the nilyr/nslyr layer axes. The Fortran state is the layer enthalpy (zqin, zqsn; icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1155-1156) with temperatures recovered by icepack_mushy_temperature_mush (icepack_mushy_physics.F90:348-452) for the ice and icepack_enthalpy_snow/temperature_snow (F90:145-179) for the snow; this model carries qicen/qsnon as states and recovers zTin/zTsn through the same laws. Heat conduction: the Fortran assembles and solves an implicit backward-Euler tridiagonal for the surface and layer temperatures (the mushy two-stage solver, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:1800-1985 with the kh conductances F90:1928-2061); this model writes the equivalent energy-conserving semi-discrete (method-of-lines) form d(q_k)/dt = (kh_up*(T_up - T_k) + kh_dn*(T_dn - T_k) + Iswabs_k)/hilyr with the interface conductances kh of the mushy conductance block (F90:1989-2061: kh_top = 2*kslyr/hslyr F90:2042, kh_snowice = 2*kslyr*kilyr(1)/(kslyr*hilyr + kilyr(1)*hslyr) F90:2046-2048, kh_bot = 2*kilyr(nilyr)/hilyr F90:2060, interior harmonic means F90:2052-2054) and the per-layer absorbed shortwave of the dEdd solver (Iswabs/Sswabs, deferred to the delta-Eddington rewrite, carried as parameters), i.e. the continuous PDE rho*cp*dT/dt = d/dz(k dT/dz) + S in enthalpy form; the layer conductivity is the mush law km = phi*(kb - ki) + ki of heat_conductivity (icepack_mushy_physics.F90:476-494; the ktherm = 1 MU71/bubbly laws remain as alternates in cice_templates.esm and are not used here). The surface temperature Tsfc is solved in the Fortran by the implicit surface energy balance fsurfn(Tsfc) - fcondtopn = 0 (the convergence checks fcondtop - fsurfn < ferrmax of the mushy two-stage solver, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:535/588/834/892, with fcondtop = 2*ks(1)*(Tsf - zTsn(1))/hslyr of F90:1674-1680 and the top-melt closure etop_mlt = max((fsurfn - fcondtopn)*dt, 0) of icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1337-1338; the downward-positive fcondtopn enters the surface heat budget as -fcondtopn, so the converged solve has fsurfn = fcondtopn); the balance is transcendental in Tsfc (the saturation-humidity exponential), so the skeleton carries Tsfc as a parameter fed by the coupled solve (stage-3 wiring). Growth/melt closures of thickness_changes (icepack_therm_vertical.F90): the melt enthalpies qmlt = enthalpy_of_melting(zSin) and qm = zqin - qmlt (F90:1283-1287), the congelation enthalpy qbot = qbotm - qbotw with qbotm = enthalpy_mush_liquid_fraction(Tbot, phi_i_mushy) and qbotw = enthalpy_brine(sst) under congel_freeze = 'one-step' (F90:1413-1416), the top/basal melt closures dhi = etop_mlt/qm(1) and ebot_mlt/qm(nilyr) (F90:1565-1581, 1589-1603), the snow/ice sublimation-condensation closures with qsub = zqsn(1) - rhos*Lvap over snow and qm(1) - rhoi*Lvap over ice (F90:1355-1403, 1502-1559), and the ocean heat flux fhocnn = fbot + (esub + etop_mlt + ebot_mlt)/dt + emlt_ocn/dt with emlt_ocn = -(qbotw*congeln + qmlt(1)*(melttn + evapin/rhoi) + qmlt(nilyr)*meltbn) (F90:1419, 1401, 1571, 1595, 1630, 1917; max(zqin, qmlt) = qmlt in the run regime since qm < 0 at melt). Radiation: the dEdd surface laws of icepack_shortwave.F90 - the snow fraction of shortwave_dEdd_set_snow (F90:3448-3454, hs0 = 0.0 so fs in {0,1}), the effective pond area of shortwave_dEdd_set_eff for tr_pond_sealvl (F90:3495-3637), the band albedos alvdrn/alidrn/alvdfn/alidfn (outputs of the deferred compute_dEdd_3bd solve, F90:1677-2936, carried as parameters), the component albedos albicen/albsnon/albpndn of F90:1496-1498 (the band-weighted sums of the awtvdr/awtidr/awtvdf/awtidf weights, icepack_parameters.F90:218-221; exact for the run's fs in {0,1} and apeffn = 0 surface-type masks), and the conservation fswintn = swabs - fswsfc - fswthrun with swabs = sum(sw*(1-al)) and fswthrun = sum of the four band transmissions. Melt ponds: the 'hlid' sea-level scheme of compute_ponds_sealvl (icepack_meltpond_sealvl.F90:50-265) with the Stefan lid growth/melt; dvn carries the per-step dvpondn and the pond tracers apnd/hpnd/ipnd/dhsn/ffracn are carried as parameters fed by the coupling (stage 3), with only the set_eff apeffn law pinned by tests. The surface-flux block (surface_heat_flux, icepack_therm_shared.F90:109-167; frzmlt_bottom_lateral, F90:637-678) is unchanged from the ktherm = 1 skeleton, with the run's emissivity = 0.95 (forcing_nml override, bugs.md #11). The ocean flux laws are the corrected rate forms of F90:510-521: freshn = -(rhoi*(congeln + meltbn + melttn) + rhos*meltsn) and fsaltn = -rhoi*dhi*ice_ref_salinity*0.001 with dhi = congeln + meltbn + melttn + evapin/rhoi (the evapn and new-snowfall terms of freshn = evapn - (rhoi*dhi + rhos*dhs) cancel exactly, F90:510-513, 1641-1672), the per-category snow thickness rate dsnown = fsnow/rhos - meltsn + evapsn/rhos, and the cell-level merged aggregates of icepack_flux.F90:196-257 (aice, fsurf, fcondtop, fhocn, fresh, fsalt, flwout, fsens, flat, evap, fswabs, fswthru, fswint, congel, meltb, meltt, melts, dsnow as sum_n(aicen*xn), with the flwout emissivity correction flwout = sum_n((flwoutn - 0.05*flw)*aicen) of F90:209-211 and the rain drainage fresh = fresh + frain*aice of icepack_therm_itd.F90:2043). The delta-Eddington solver (compute_dEdd_3bd, icepack_shortwave.F90:1677-3389) and the mushy enthalpy/T inversion pinning are deferred; see README.md for the coverage table.",
   "tags": [
    "cryosphere",
    "sea-ice",
    "cice",
    "thermodynamics",
    "radiation",
    "cesm"
   ],
   "created": "2026-11-01T00:00:00Z",
   "authors": [
    "EqESM project contributors"
   ],
   "references": [
    {
     "citation": "Hunke, E. C., Allard, R., Bailey, D. A., Blain, P., Craig, A., Dupont, F., ... & Roberts, A. F. (2023). CICE-Consortium Icepack v1.2.4 and CICE v6.3.22: documentation and user's guide. Los Alamos National Laboratory (LA-UR-23-31851)."
    },
    {
     "citation": "CESM (Community Earth System Model), ESCOMP/CESM: CICE sea-ice source (cesm3_cice6_6_3_22) - icepack_shortwave.F90, icepack_therm_mushy.F90, icepack_mushy_physics.F90, icepack_therm_vertical.F90, icepack_flux.F90, icepack_meltpond_sealvl.F90, icepack_therm_itd.F90 - the reference implementation these components are transcribed from.",
     "url": "https://github.com/ESCOMP/CESM"
    },
    {
     "citation": "EarthSciModels - the authoritative .esm corpus this component lives in.",
     "url": "https://github.com/EarthSciML/EarthSciModels"
    }
   ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "ncat": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_CAT"
  },
  "ice_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_ILYR"
  },
  "snow_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_SLYR"
  }
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_CAT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 5,
   "description": "number of ice thickness categories (namelist ncat = 5), [-]"
  },
  "N_ILYR": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 8,
   "description": "number of ice layers (namelist nilyr = 8 in the D-class run), [-]"
  },
  "N_SLYR": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "number of snow layers (namelist nslyr = 3 in the D-class run), [-]"
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "Thermodynamics": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "./cice_templates.esm"
    }
   ],
   "variables": {
    "qicen": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "ice layer enthalpy (zqin, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1155), the conserved vertical thermo state for the mushy (ktherm = 2) thermodynamics, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qsnon": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "snow_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "default": 0.0,
     "description": "snow layer enthalpy (zqsn, F90:1156), [J/m3]"
    },
    "Tmlts": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "layer liquidus temperature of the mushy thermodynamics, Tmlts = liquidus_temperature_mush(zSin) (icepack_mushy_physics.F90:227-261, the Assur 1958 liquidus), [C]"
    },
    "zTin": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "internal ice layer temperatures recovered from the enthalpy (icepack_mushy_temperature_mush, icepack_mushy_physics.F90:348-452, the piecewise quadratic inversion of the Assur liquidus), [C]"
    },
    "zTsn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "snow_layer"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "internal snow layer temperatures recovered from the enthalpy (icepack_enthalpy_snow/temperature_snow, icepack_mushy_physics.F90:145-179; fresh snow), [C]"
    },
    "hi": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "description": "total ice thickness per category hi = vicen/aicen (compute_ponds_sealvl, icepack_meltpond_sealvl.F90:134), zeroed for open-water categories (aicen <= puny), [m]"
    },
    "hs": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "description": "snow depth per category hs = vsnon/aicen (F90:135), zeroed for open-water categories, [m]"
    },
    "hilyr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "description": "ice layer thickness hilyr = hi/nilyr, [m]"
    },
    "hslyr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m",
     "description": "snow layer thickness hslyr = hs/nslyr, [m]"
    },
    "kilyr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "thermal conductivity at ice layer midpoints, the mushy heat_conductivity km = phi*(kb - ki) + ki with phi the liquid fraction (icepack_mushy_physics.F90:476-494, ki = 2.3 and kb = 0.5375 F90:62-63); the ktherm = 2 law, [W/m/K]"
    },
    "kslyr": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "snow conductivity kslyr = ksno = 0.30 (conductivity_snow_array, icepack_mushy_physics.F90:130-139; icepack_parameters.F90:90), [W/m/K]"
    },
    "kilyr_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "conductivity of ice layer 1 (gather kilyr(:,1)), [W/m/K]"
    },
    "kilyr_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m/K",
     "description": "conductivity of the bottom ice layer (gather kilyr(:,nilyr)), [W/m/K]"
    },
    "zTin_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "temperature of ice layer 1 (gather zTin(:,1)), the snow-ice interface temperature, [C]"
    },
    "zTin_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "temperature of the bottom ice layer (gather zTin(:,nilyr)), [C]"
    },
    "zTsn_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "temperature of the top snow layer (gather zTsn(:,1)), the temperature the top conductive flux fcondtopn is taken against (fcondtop = 2*ks(1)*(Tsf - zTsn(1))/hslyr, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:1677; icepack_therm_bl99.F90:402), [C]"
    },
    "zTsn_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "temperature of the bottom snow layer (gather zTsn(:,nslyr)), the snow-ice interface temperature feeding the ice top boundary flux, [C]"
    },
    "qsnon_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "enthalpy of snow layer 1 (gather qsnon(:,1)), the snow melt enthalpy zqsn(1), [J/m3]"
    },
    "qmlt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "melt enthalpy of the mush from the layer bulk salinity, qmlt(k) = enthalpy_of_melting(zSin(k)) = cp_ocn*rhow*liquidus_temperature_mush(zSin(k)) (icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1283, the ktherm = 2 branch; icepack_mushy_physics.F90:313-325), [J/m3]"
    },
    "qm": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat",
      "ice_layer"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "meltable enthalpy per layer qm(k) = zqin(k) - qmlt(k) (icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1287), the ktherm = 2 denominator of the growth/melt closures, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qm_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "meltable enthalpy of ice layer 1 (gather qm(:,1)), the top-melt and ice-sublimation enthalpy, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qm_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "meltable enthalpy of the bottom ice layer (gather qm(:,nilyr)), the bottom-melt enthalpy, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qmlt_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "melt enthalpy of ice layer 1 (gather qmlt(:,1)), the emlt_ocn weight of the top melt and sublimation, [J/m3]"
    },
    "qmlt_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "melt enthalpy of the bottom ice layer (gather qmlt(:,nilyr)), the emlt_ocn weight of the bottom melt, [J/m3]"
    },
    "kh_top": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2/K",
     "description": "conductance at the top snow surface kh(1) = 2*kslyr/hslyr (the mushy conductance block, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:2042; identical to the ktherm = 1 form, icepack_therm_bl99.F90:930), [W/m2/K]"
    },
    "kh_snowice": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2/K",
     "description": "conductance at the snow-ice interface kh(1+nslyr) = 2*kslyr*kilyr(1)/(kslyr*hilyr + kilyr(1)*hslyr) (F90:2046-2048), [W/m2/K]"
    },
    "kh_bot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2/K",
     "description": "conductance at the bottom ice surface kh(1+nslyr+nilyr) = 2*kilyr(nilyr)/hilyr (F90:2060), [W/m2/K]"
    },
    "Tbot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "degC",
     "description": "ice bottom temperature, the ocean freezing temperature at sss under tfrz_option = 'mushy' (frzmlt_bottom_lateral sets Tbot = Tf, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:650; the Assur-1958 liquidus of icepack_sea_freezing_temperature, icepack_therm_shared.F90:404-406), [C]"
    },
    "Qsfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "description": "saturated surface specific humidity over ice (surface_heat_flux, icepack_therm_shared.F90:152-154), [kg/kg]"
    },
    "fsensn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "downward sensible heat flux fsensn = shcoef*(potT - TsfK) (F90:161), [W/m2]"
    },
    "flatn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "downward latent heat flux flatn = lhcoef*(Qa - Qsfc) (F90:162), [W/m2]"
    },
    "flwoutn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "upward longwave flux flwoutn = -emissivity*stefan_boltzmann*TsfK^4 (F90:158), [W/m2]"
    },
    "fsurfn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "net flux to the top surface excluding fcondtopn (surface_heat_flux, F90:147-165), [W/m2]"
    },
    "ustar": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "skin friction velocity for the ocean heat flux, ustar = max(sqrt(sqrt(strocnxT^2 + strocnyT^2)/rhow), ustar_min) (frzmlt_bottom_lateral, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:665-666; ustar_min = 0.005, icepack_parameters.F90:99), [m/s]"
    },
    "fbot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "heat flux from the ocean to the ice bottom (frzmlt_bottom_lateral, F90:662-678; 0.006 transfer coefficient F90:674), [W/m2]"
    },
    "fcondtopn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "downward conductive flux at the top surface fcondtopn = kh(1)*(Tsfc - zTsn(1)) taken against the TOP snow layer (fcondtop = 2*ks(1)*(Tsf - zTsn(1))/hslyr, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:1677; icepack_therm_bl99.F90:401-404), [W/m2]"
    },
    "fsurf_bal": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "surface energy balance residual fsurf_bal = fsurfn - fcondtopn: the converged implicit solve of the mushy two-stage solver has fsurfn = fcondtopn (same sign) to within ferrmax = 1e-3 W m-2, the consistency checks fcondtop - fsurfn < ferrmax of icepack_therm_mushy.F90:535/588/834/892 and the top-melt closure etop_mlt = max((fsurfn - fcondtopn)*dt, 0) of icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1337-1338 (downward-positive fcondtopn enters as -fcondtopn in the surface heat budget); a diagnostic for the balance pins (the .esm carries Tsfc as a parameter, so the residual is measured, not solved), [W/m2]"
    },
    "fcondbotn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "downward conductive flux at the bottom surface fcondbotn = kh(1+nslyr+nilyr)*(zTin(nilyr) - Tbot) (fcondbot = 2*km(nilyr)*(zTin(nilyr) - Tbot)/hilyr, F90:1660), [W/m2]"
    },
    "esub": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^2",
     "description": "energy available for sublimation esub = max(-flatn*dt, 0) (thickness_changes, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1333-1334), [J/m2]"
    },
    "econ": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^2",
     "description": "energy available for condensation econ = min(-flatn*dt, 0) (F90:1335), [J/m2]"
    },
    "etop_mlt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^2",
     "description": "energy available for top melt etop_mlt = max((fsurfn - fcondtopn)*dt, 0) (F90:1337-1338), [J/m2]"
    },
    "ebot_mlt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^2",
     "description": "energy available for bottom melt ebot_mlt = max((fcondbotn - fbot)*dt, 0) (F90:1340-1341), [J/m2]"
    },
    "ebot_gro": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^2",
     "description": "energy available for bottom growth ebot_gro = min((fcondbotn - fbot)*dt, 0) (F90:1342), [J/m2]"
    },
    "qbotm": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "enthalpy of the congelation ice forming at the bottom, qbotm = enthalpy_mush_liquid_fraction(Tbot, phi_i_mushy) (icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1413, the congel_freeze = 'one-step' branch; icepack_mushy_physics.F90:293-307), [J/m3]"
    },
    "qbotw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "enthalpy of the brine rejected to the ocean during congelation, qbotw = enthalpy_brine(sst) (F90:1414; icepack_mushy_physics.F90:330-342), [J/m3]"
    },
    "qbot": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "J/m^3",
     "description": "enthalpy of new congelation ice growing at the bottom qbot = qbotm - qbotw (F90:1415-1416, the one-step denominator), [J/m3]"
    },
    "congeln": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "basal ice growth rate congel = ebot_gro/qbot per step (F90:1444), in continuous rate form /dt, [m/s]"
    },
    "meltbn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "basal ice melt rate, the bottom-melt closure dhi = ebot_mlt/qm(nilyr) (F90:1589-1603 with qm = zqin - qmlt, F90:1287), in continuous rate form; the Fortran cascades the energy bottom-up over the layers with the min(-dzi, ...) clamps, [m/s]"
    },
    "melttn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "top ice melt rate, the top-melt closure dhi = etop_mlt/qm(1) (F90:1565-1581 with qm = zqin - qmlt); the Fortran first melts the snow with etop_mlt (F90:1523-1544) and cascades the remainder over the ice layers, [m/s]"
    },
    "meltsn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "snow melt rate, the snow top-melt closure dhs = etop_mlt/zqsn(1) (F90:1527), in continuous rate form; the hs > puny guard mirrors the snow-first cascade of the condensation/sublimation closures (F90:1338-1340) -- a category with no snow (hs <= puny) has dzs(1) ~ 0 and the Fortran clamp dhs = max(-dzs(1), etop_mlt/zqsn(1)) (F90:1530) pins its melt to ~0, [m/s]"
    },
    "dsnown": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "m/s",
     "description": "snow thickness change rate dsnown = fsnow/rhos - meltsn + evapsn/rhos: the new snowfall hsn_new = fsnow*dt/rhos and the snow closures dzs = -meltsn - evapsn/rhos (F90:1641-1653, 1664-1672); the merged cell-level dsnow = sum(aicen*dsnown) reproduces the vsnon change, [m/s]"
    },
    "evapn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "description": "ice/snow mass sublimated (negative) or condensed (positive), evapn = (esub + econ)/qsub per step with the vapor enthalpy qsub = zqsn(1) - rhos*Lvap over snow or qm(1) - rhoi*Lvap over ice: the Fortran condensation closure dhs = econ/qsub adds econ = -flatn*dt to the same evapn accumulator as the sublimation closure dhs = esub/qsub (F90:1355-1403, 1502-1521, 1546-1559; Lvap = 2.501e6, icepack_parameters.F90:84), so the net is evapn = -flatn*dt/qsub = -flatn/qsub in rate form; in continuous rate form, [kg/m2/s]"
    },
    "evapsn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "description": "snow sublimation part of evapn (evapsn accumulates when snow is present, F90:1520-1521); the skeleton's split follows the snow-first cascade, [kg/m2/s]"
    },
    "evapin": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "description": "ice sublimation part of evapn (F90:1398-1399, 1557-1558), evapin = evapn - evapsn, [kg/m2/s]"
    },
    "emlt_ocn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "total energy of the brine transferred to the ocean, in rate form emlt_ocn = -(qbotw*congeln + qmlt(1)*(melttn + evapin/rhoi) + qmlt(nilyr)*meltbn): the congelation rejection -qbotw*dhi (F90:1419), the condensation/melt-water -qmlt(1)*dhi of the vapor closures (F90:1401, 1559), and -max(zqin,qmlt)*dhi of the top and bottom melt closures (F90:1571, 1595; max(zqin,qmlt) = qmlt in the run regime since qm = zqin - qmlt < 0 at melt), all per-step energies divided by dt, [W/m2]"
    },
    "freshn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "description": "fresh water flux to the ocean, in rate form freshn = evapn - (rhoi*dhi + rhos*dhs) with the net thickness changes dhi = congeln + meltbn + melttn + evapin/rhoi and dhs = meltsn + evapsn/rhos (F90:510-513 with dhi = hin - worki and dhs = hsn - works - hsn_new of F90:1664-1672); the sublimation/condensation terms cancel exactly (evapn = evapin + evapsn), and the new snowfall hsn_new = fsnow*dt/rhos also cancels (added to dzs(1) before hin/hsn are summed, F90:1641-1653), leaving freshn = -(rhoi*(congeln + meltbn + melttn) + rhos*meltsn); the rain is added separately at the cell level (fresh = fresh + frain*aice, icepack_therm_itd.F90:2043), [kg/m2/s]"
    },
    "fsaltn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "kg/m^2/s",
     "description": "salt flux to the ocean under saltflux_option = 'constant', in rate form fsaltn = -rhoi*dhi*ice_ref_salinity*0.001 with the same net thickness change dhi = congeln + meltbn + melttn + evapin/rhoi as freshn (F90:513, 521; ice_ref_salinity = 4, icepack_parameters.F90:87), [kg/m2/s]"
    },
    "fhocnn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "net heat flux to the ocean fhocnn = fbot + (esub + etop_mlt + ebot_mlt)/dt + emlt_ocn, the ocean heat left after use by the ice (F90:1625-1630 with einex_sfc_flux = 0 and vapor_flux_correction = .false., plus the ktherm = 2 brine-energy term emlt_ocn/dt of F90:1917), [W/m2]"
    },
    "snowfracn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
      "ncat"
     ],
     "units": "1",
     "description": "horizontal snow fraction used for radiation, snowfracn = min(fs, 1 - apeffn) with fs from shortwave_dEdd_set_snow (icepack_shortwave.F90:3448-3454) and the pond-reduced fsn = min(fsn, 1 - fpn) of shortwave_dEdd_set_eff (F90:3632; run_dEdd F90:1185), [-]"
    },
    "apeffn": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "shape": [
