     "id": "thermo_surface_fluxes_step1_cell3_5",
     "description": "Instantaneous pins of the step-1 surface energy-block aggregates against cice_thermo_flux.csv row (step 1, i=3, j=5): the model's per-category flwoutn = -emissivity*stefan_boltzmann*(Tsfc+273.15)^4 with the D-class run's emissivity = 0.95 (forcing_nml override, bugs.md #11) and fsensn = shcoef*(potT - (Tsfc+273.15)), aggregated by the cell-level laws flwout = sum_n((flwoutn - 0.05*flw)*aicen) and fsens = sum_n(fsensn*aicen) (icepack_flux.F90:204, 209-211). The transfer coefficients shcoef/lhcoef are the similarity chain of the coupling cap's atmo_boundary_layer (icepack_atmo.F90:52-389, the natmiter = 5 unroll) driven by the ENTRY Tsfcn and the d_entr uvelT/vvelT of the uarea-weighted U-point reconstruction (grid_average_X2YA, ice_step_mod.F90:126); the fluxes are then evaluated at the EXIT Tsfcn (the converged implicit surface-energy solve), with flw/potT/Qa/rhoa from cice_run_imports.csv. The tolerance is 1e-9 rather than 1e-12 because the merged dump values are the icepack_flux.F90 sums over the thickness distribution taken at the flux merge with the ENTRY aicen (merge_fluxes, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:3169, aicen_init), while this test aggregates with the exit aicen: at (3,5) the linear_itd remap changes aicen by <= 1.8e-5, so the exit-weighting approximates the dump to ~1e-10 (the solve-vs-exit Tsfc residual is ~1e-7..3e-6 K, which also contributes; the step-1 fswsfc is unpinnable, albedo_dump(0) does not exist).",
