    {
     "id": "thermo_surface_fluxes_step1_cell2_4",
     "description": "Instantaneous pins of the step-1 surface energy-block aggregates flwout and flat against cice_thermo_flux.csv row (step 1, i=2, j=4): the model's per-category flwoutn = -emissivity*stefan_boltzmann*(Tsfc+273.15)^4 (emissivity = 0.95, forcing_nml override, bugs.md #11) and flatn = lhcoef*(Qa - Qsfc_ice(Tsfc, rhoa)) (the latent heat flux of the coupling cap's surface_heat_flux, icepack_therm_shared.F90:147-165), aggregated by the cell-level laws flwout = sum_n((flwoutn - 0.05*flw)*aicen) and flat = sum_n(flatn*aicen) (icepack_flux.F90:204, 209-211, 218). The merged dump values are the icepack_flux.F90 sums evaluated at the flux merge with the ENTRY aicen (merge_fluxes, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:3169, aicen_init) at the converged implicit surface-energy solve; this test evaluates at the EXIT Tsfcn (the exit-dump Tsfc differs from the solve Tsfc by ~1e-7..3e-6 K, the linear_itd tracer-remap residual, so the fluxes carry a ~1e-9..1e-7 relative residual -- observed 2.6e-9 for flwout, 1.0e-7 for flat). The transfer coefficients shcoef/lhcoef are the similarity chain of the coupling cap's atmo_boundary_layer (icepack_atmo.F90:52-389, the natmiter = 5 unroll) driven by the ENTRY Tsfcn and the d_entr uvelT/vvelT of the uarea-weighted U-point reconstruction of the ice_ic field (grid_average_X2YA, ice_step_mod.F90:126), with flw/potT/Qa/rhoa from cice_run_imports.csv. Tolerance 1e-6 covers the solve-vs-exit Tsfc residual for flat (observed 1.0e-7); the same Si_u10-relaxation rationale as the cice_coupling.esm surface-flux pins. (The cell-level fsurf/fcondtop remain unpinnable: they need the solve-internal zTsn(1)/Tsfc; the model's fswsfc = 0 default makes fsurfn miss the dump by rel 0.78.)",
