    {
     "id": "thermo_sublimation_condensation_step1_cell2_4",
     "description": "Instantaneous pins of the step-1 sublimation/condensation aggregates evap and dsnow against cice_thermo_flux.csv row (step 1, i=2, j=4): the model's per-category evapn = (esub + econ)/qsub with esub = max(-flatn*dt, 0) and econ = min(-flatn*dt, 0) (the Fortran condensation closure dhs = econ/qsub accumulates into the same evapn as the sublimation closure dhs = esub/qsub, icepack_therm_vertical.F90:1355-1403, 1502-1521, 1546-1559, so the net is evapn = -flatn*dt/qsub) and the vapor enthalpy qsub = zqsn(1) - rhos*Lvap over snow or qm(1) - rhoi*Lvap over ice; evapsn = evapn over the snow branch and 0 over bare ice, and dsnown = fsnow/rhos - meltsn + evapsn/rhos (meltsn = 0 here: the top melt energy etop_mlt vanishes at the converged solve since fsurfn < fcondtopn, and the hs <= puny bare-ice category is guarded, F90:1530). The dump values are merged with the ENTRY aicen (merge_fluxes, F90:3169) and the closures are evaluated with the state AFTER the implicit surface-energy solve (thickness_changes runs post-solve), so this test carries the EXIT qicen/qsnon as initial_conditions and the EXIT zSin as a parameter override (the solved-state proxy; the entry state leaves evap rel 1.4e-4) with the EXIT Tsfcn and entry aicen/vicen/vsnon. The volume tendency dsnow is dumped per step [m], so the expected value is dump/dt = 7.8782234486014576e-10 m/s against the model's rate law [m/s]. Observed residuals: evap 1.2e-7, dsnow 1.1e-7, tolerance 1e-6 (the solve-vs-exit state/Tsfc residuals of the linear_itd remap; the Si_u10-relaxation rationale of cice_coupling.esm). Cell (2,4) step 1 is chosen because its remap melts thin ice rather than mixing tracers, giving the smallest solve-vs-exit residual of the dump cells; cats 2-5 are condensing (flatn > 0, dump evap = +2.0e-7 kg/m2/s) and cat 1 is a bare-ice sublimator (vsnon 2.8e-15, the ice-branch closure).",
