    {
     "id": "thermo_surface_balance_step2_cell2_4",
     "description": "Instantaneous pins of the surface energy balance residual fsurf_bal = fsurfn - fcondtopn per category against the implicit solve of the mushy two-stage solver (cell (2,4), step 2). The Fortran converges the implicit surface balance to fsurfn = fcondtopn (same sign; the fcondtop - fsurfn < ferrmax consistency checks of icepack_therm_mushy.F90:535/588/834/892 with ferrmax = 1e-3 W m-2, icepack_therm_shared.F90:42), which the model reproduces as the algebraic diagnostic fsurf_bal = fsurfn - fcondtopn with fsurfn = fswsfc + emissivity*flw - emissivity*sigma*TsfK^4 + shcoef*(potT - TsfK) + lhcoef*(Qa - Qsfc) (surface_heat_flux, icepack_therm_shared.F90:147-165) and fcondtopn = kh_top*(Tsfc - zTsn(1)) = 2*kslyr/hslyr*(Tsfc - zTsn(1)) (F90:1677, 2042). The state is the dumped EXIT state (the exit dump runs after step_therm2 + update_state, CICE_RunMod.F90:267-273, so the residual measures the solve closure plus the post-solve bottom-melt regrid shifts; meltb(2) = 8.76e-4 m), with the EXIT Tsfcn and the ENTRY aicen/vicen/vsnon (the merge weights and the hs = vsnon/aicen snow depth of the conductance). The shortwave is the step-2 consumed dEdd surface absorption fswsfc(2) = fswsfcn(albedo dump step 1) * netsw(2)/netsw(1) (the prep_radiation rescale, icepack_shortwave.F90:3893-3922, pinned to round-off by the thermo_radiation_scale_* tests; netsw(1) = the step-1 cice_flux exit scale_factor saved by coupling_prep, CICE_RunMod.F90:618-624), and shcoef/lhcoef are the similarity atmo_boundary_layer coefficients at the ENTRY Tsfcn with the uarea-weighted ice_ic uvelT (grid_average_X2YA, ice_step_mod.F90:114-128; the ice velocity ~1e-4 m/s is negligible against the wind ~2.7 m/s). Cat 1 is skipped: vsnon = 0 exactly at entry (bare ice), where the .esm kh_top = 2*kslyr/hslyr diverges (hslyr = 0) while the Fortran switches to the bare-ice branch kcstar(1) = km(1) (calc_intercell_conductivity, icepack_therm_mushy.F90:2038-2051). Measured residuals at the exit state: 6.8e-4 (cat 2), 6.7e-3 (cat 3), 2.0e-3 (cat 4), 8.8e-4 (cat 5) W m-2 - the ferrmax solve tolerance plus the step-2 bottom-melt regrid shifts (the dumped merged solve residual is fsurf - fcondtop = -3.3e-10 W m-2, cice_thermo_flux.csv); the absolute tolerance 2e-2 is ~3x the largest measured. The step-1 balance is NOT pinned: the step-1 thermo consumed the init-time dEdd solve (init_shortwave, CICE_InitMod.F90:192-201) which the dumps do not contain, and the step-1 albedo-dump shortwave leaves the residual at ~-15 W m-2.",
