    {
     "id": "thermo_radiation_scale_step2_cell3_5",
     "description": "Instantaneous pins of the step-2 radiation conservation aggregates against cice_thermo_flux.csv row (step 2, i=3, j=5), testing the prep_radiation rescale of icepack_shortwave.F90:3893-3922: the step-2 thermo consumed the STORED step-1 dEdd outputs (cice_albedo.csv step 1) rescaled by scale_factor = netsw(2)/netsw(1), where netsw(S) = sum_bands sw(S)*(1 - al_band_ai) with the grid-box-mean albedos al_band_ai = sum_n(aicen*al_bandn) per unit grid area (the quirky aggregation of F90:3902-3922, NOT /aice), netsw(1) = the step-1 cice_flux exit scale_factor saved by coupling_prep ('Save net shortwave', CICE_RunMod.F90:618-624) = 64.04556363, and netsw(2) computed from the step-2 imported bands and the step-1 albedo state = 53.7212879 (ratio = 0.838797956614586). The model reproduces the scaled per-category values as the step-1 bands times the ratio with the unchanged step-1 albedos (the dEdd solve is linear in the incoming bands; only the fswsfc/fswthru_* outputs are rescaled, F90:3905-3922), and the aggregates fswabs = sum_n(aicen*sum_bands(sw*(1-al))) and fswthru = sum_n(aicen*sum_bands fswthru_*) use the entry aicen(2) = albedo_dump(1) aicen (the post-dynamics state of step 1), reproducing the merged dump values to round-off.",
